# Results: visual first

In Results (thesis Ch 7, paper §6), put the figure or table immediately after the one-sentence claim, then write only what the visual cannot say.

- One claim, then the artefact, then at most the high-ROI cell (the one that moves, or the number that is not on the page).
- Do not restate every bar, CI, or table row in the body.
- Holm \(p\) is the Holm-adjusted paired \(t\). Wilcoxon \(p\) is raw. Never write “Wilcoxon Holm”.
- Dataset A display name is **condition aggregation**. Never Path A/B, equal-n neighbourhood, or condition state.
- Results report numbers. Discussion interprets.

This is paper UX, not decoration: a reader should be able to get the pattern from the visual without holding six CIs.
